> `22-42`: **Fix missing `value` field and invalid return action in unist-util-visit v5**
> 
> The replacement node violates the mdast spec: `Code` nodes require a `value` field (mdast Literal interface). Additionally, `unist-util-visit` v5 only supports return actions `true` (CONTINUE), `false` (EXIT), or `'skip'` (SKIP)—returning a number like `index + 1` is not a valid action and won't control traversal as intended.
> 
> <details>
> <summary>Proposed fix</summary>
> 
> ```diff
>  export function remarkMermaidBypass() {
>    return (tree) => {
>      visit(tree, "code", (node, index, parent) => {
>        if (node.lang === "mermaid-render") {
> +        if (!parent || !Array.isArray(parent.children) || typeof index !== "number") {
> +          return;
> +        }
> +
>          const newNode = {
>            type: "code",
> +          value: typeof node.value === "string" ? node.value : "",
>            data: {
>              hName: "pre",
